Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:48:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gbm: tell the user when an HDR TV input is in its HDMI 1.4
 compatibility mode

An HDR TV whose input is left in its HDMI 1.4 compatibility mode (LG:
"HDMI Deep Colour" off) presents an EDID without an HDMI Forum block,
whose preferred mode is 2160p30 and which offers 2160p50/60 only as
YCbCr 4:2:0. Kodi then starts its GUI at 30 Hz, which feels slow, and
nvidia-drm lists no 2160p mode above 30 Hz at all. Nothing told the user
why: on an LG C5 the first two starts of a new installation ran at
2160p30 until the TV itself turned the setting on.

CDisplayInfo::UhdLimitedToHdmi14() recognizes that state from the raw
EDID: a YCbCr 4:2:0 Video Data Block with 2160p50/60 and no HDMI Forum
block, in a display with HDR static metadata or Dolby Vision (an HDR TV
has inputs for the full HDMI 2.0 rate; a 2014 TV limited to 4:2:0 has no
HDR). CWinSystemGbm then shows a notification after the skin is loaded:
at start, and when a video starts and the display has entered that
state. It says to restart afterwards, because the modes of the display
are read only at start.

The text is a core string (English, 39995) with its Spanish translations
in Estuary (31693), as the other Hades texts.
